```

Clicking a token opens its **ICP market**, rather than forcing the user to think about pair terminology.

For example:

```text
ckUSDC
ckUSDC / ICP
```

The pair still exists technically, but **don't make it the product's mental model**.

### Most important: New

Your discovery page should be:

```text
NEW ON ICP

New Tokens
────────────────────────────

TOKEN    PRICE    LIQUIDITY   AGE   VOLUME

ABC      $0.002   $18K         4m    $32K
XYZ      $0.018   $42K         18m   $91K
...
```

Then:

```text
TRENDING ON ICP
```

```text
TOKEN     PRICE     24H       VOLUME
PIKO      $0.021    +42%      $93K
CHAT      $0.084    +20%      $41K
...
```

This makes ICPay feel like:

> **“The market terminal for ICP assets.”**

rather than:

> “Another DEX pair browser.”

And because ICP's ledger/index architecture is standardized around canisters and ICRC assets, you can build the backend around **token/ledger canister IDs** rather than hard-coding pair concepts. ([ICP Developer Docs][2])

**I think this is the cleaner direction for ICPay.** Your current trading screen can stay almost exactly as it is; the main improvement is changing the **information architecture and discovery layer** around ICP tokens.

